      "width": 1200,
      "height": 542,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "NPS Photo",
      "description": "A partly-deteriorated rectangular structure of brick and stone stands at the edge of a shallow waterway.\nDuring the Armory era, the former hydroelectric plant was known as the Rolling Mill. After that, it was the Harpers Ferry Paper Company. The structure, which sits on a foundation that originally dates to the 1834 tilt-hammer shop, symbolizes over 200 years of water-powered industry in Harpers Ferry.\nKeywords: cultural landscape; rolling mill; mill; industry; armory; articles",
